    </div><dl class="sheet" data-slot="sheet"><div class="row r-value"><dt class="i-puzzle">economy of topic</dt>
<dd><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5333743">economy of Paris</a></dd>
<span class="tools">
        <span class="prov-none" title="—"></span>
        <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q90#P8744"
       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a></span>
</div></dl><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>The economy of the City of Paris is based largely on services and commerce. Of the 390,480 enterprises in Paris, 80.6 percent are engaged in commerce, transportation, and diverse services, 6.5 percent in construction, and 3.8 percent in industry. The story is similar in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Region">Paris Region</a> (Île-de-France): 76.7 percent of enterprises are engaged in commerce and services, and 3.4 percent in industry.</p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris#Economy">Economy ↗</a></div></section>
