</div></dl><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>The <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisii_(Gaul)">Parisii</a></i> people inhabited the Paris area from around the middle of the 3rd century BC. One of the area's major north–south trade routes crossed the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine">Seine</a> on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%8Ele_de_la_Cit%C3%A9">Île de la Cité</a>, which gradually became an important trading centre. The Parisii traded with many river towns, some as far away as the Iberian Peninsula, and minted their own coins.</p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris#History">History ↗</a></div><div class="topic-articles"><div class="topic-article">
    <div class="body">
        <p class="source"><img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wikipedia-logo-v2.svg?width=60" alt="" width="18"> en.wikipedia.org</p>
        <a class="title" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Paris" lang="en">History of Paris</a><p class="desc">history of the capital city of France</p></div><img class="pic k-photo"
     style="--a:1.4888"
     src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Palais%20de%20la%20Cite.jpg?width=330"
     alt=""
